sec.p:
To evaluate lymphocyte differentiation activity in CLP cells, we implemented a gene set scoring approach using Gene Ontology (GO) terms and TF databases from the AnimalTFDB68. Functional gene sets were retrieved from the Molecular Signatures Database (v7.1) database and converted to mouse orthologs using a custom mapping function. We extracted lymphocyte-related gene sets based on ‘GO:REGULATION OF LYMPHOCYTE ACTIVATION’69 and ‘GO:LYMPHOCYTE DIFFERENTIATION’69. Genes shared between these lymphocyte-associated pathways and the TF list were retained to define a set of lymphocyte-specific TFs. For each cell, a lymphocyte-differentiation score was calculated by averaging normalized expression levels across the selected markers:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
